WP4 — flake reproduced, fixed, removed
  -----------------------------------
  Flake A (observed, real): test_resilience.py::TestBreakerRegistry::test_reset_all_restores_closed
    Root cause: WP2 vault-probe test leaves global VAULT_CB failure_count=1 -> trip loop hits
      CircuitOpenError instead of expected RuntimeError (order-dependent shared-state leak).
    Fix: conftest.py autouse fixture calls reset_all_breakers() before/after every test
      (breaker state scoped per-test; not a retry wrapper).
    Proof: pytest tests/test_probe_scheduler.py tests/test_resilience.py -q -> 39 passed

  Flake B (named in directive, reproduced only with real PG):
    tests/test_migration_v004.py::TestV004Postgres::test_up_adds_column_when_missing
      psycopg2.errors.DuplicateTable: relation "trades" already exists
    Root cause: bare CREATE TABLE "trades" in shared traderos_test colliding with the `trades`
      relation bootstrapped earlier by the Postgres repository layer (test/order-dependent).
    Fix: pg_conn fixture drops `trades` BEFORE and AFTER each test (per-test ownership of the name).
    Proof with PG up: full suite x2 -> 1566 passed / 7 skipped both runs (was 1 failed).

  Flake C (named, never reproduced in 7 full runs this session): test_ha_failover subprocess SIGTERM
    drill under full-suite load -> passes in isolation and under load; no marker added.

